// rt_out_count — cardinality of the current result set.
//
// The read API returns a SET, and it returns it in the named result store
// rather than as an M1 value. That is unchanged and still deliberate: building
// an M1 list by repeated list_append names the accumulating list at every call
// site, and every mention of a list is a deep copy (Value::List is a plain
// Vec<Value>), so materializing an R-element result would cost O(R^2). The
// caller reads the set by cardinality plus rt_out_at / rt_out_has, all cheap.
//
// PHASE A: the store is a stride-3 u32v, so the cardinality is its own length
// over three — no set_len, no hash table. THIS IS EXACT ONLY BECAUSE
// rt_out_emit DEDUPS ON THE WAY IN. An array that admitted duplicates would
// make this a RECORD count, and the fixture's deliberate double-index is what
// pins the difference.
fn rt_out_count(u: Unit) -> Int {
  let n = u32v_len(Text("rt:out"))
  int_div(n, Int(3))
}
